<title>USA: Atalanta/Sosnoff drops plan to go private.</title>
<headline>Atalanta/Sosnoff drops plan to go private.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atalanta/Sosnoff Capital Corp said on Monday that Martin Sosnoff, the company's chief executive officer, had abandoned an effort to take the company private.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said that an independent committee looking at the proposal had been disbanded and that its authority had been terminated.</p>
<p>The independent committee, composed of non-management company directors, had determined that until it received a report from its financial advisor it was not in a position to consider the proposal by Sosnoff on the potential privatization, the statement said.</p>
</text>
